title: What Power Do We Want
subtitle: The system of government PPS stands for.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && !!Q.polish_party_rules && PolishParty.stanceAvailable(Q, 'form_of_power') !}
on-arrival: {!
// Card party.form_of_power (catalogue 4.4; technical reference 10.8): 1 T, 0 R, the card then waits 6 months. Z — 0.51: the present line can be
// confirmed for 1 T and the usual wait; returning the card to the hand is free.
PolishParty.stanceView(Q, 'form_of_power');
!}

= What Power Do We Want

The present line: **[+ pl_stance_current +]**. A new declaration costs this month's action; it changes no law in force and gives no reform by itself.

- @parliamentarism
- @strong_presidency
- @workers_councils
- @easy_discard

@parliamentarism
title: Parliamentarism
subtitle: [? if pl_stance_parliamentarism_present = 1 : This is the present line. Confirming it costs this month's action and the card waits as after a change; nothing else changes. ?][? if pl_stance_parliamentarism_present = 0 : The way of majorities, cabinet responsibility and democratisation. ?]
choose-if: {! return PolishParty.stanceStatus(Q, 'form_of_power', 'parliamentarism').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_stance_parliamentarism_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishParty.stanceChoose(Q, 'form_of_power', 'parliamentarism');
!}
go-to: result

